 ## Overview
-Bounding Wall Contour Overlay is a non-photorealistic visualization technique that displays line contours of a reference scalar field on the vertical bounding walls of a 3D volume [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of providing spatial context for deformed interfaces (such as billows or panels) without occluding the primary data or introducing visual clutter [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that render edges within the volume or in image space, this method projects 2D contour lines onto the 3D scene's boundary planes, ensuring the annotations are read as context rather than competing data surfaces [S1, unofficial].
